If there is just the image, it works; the generated code passes the element correctly:
```js
var img = root();

$.handle_lazy_img(img);
```

With an additional element, no variable for the image is generated and the call becomes empty 🤔
```js
var fragment = root();

$.next(2);
$.handle_lazy_img();
```

I guess a check is missing to get an element reference in case there isn't one yet. E.g. [passing in a `src` attribute](https://svelte.dev/playground/fd9fd756b9c942f18f5c9364a8c46454?version=5.1.13#H4sIAAAAAAAACm2PwUrEMBRFfyW-zSh0Gmdb24LMxp3gQhAjkiZvpnHSJOS96TiW_ruUUVduD-dwuRMEPSBU8IDeR3GK2VtxjdYx2hsoYOc8ElSvE_A5Ld4CoPit7lMqaUTPC-s04X_cxMAYmKCCmkx2iVsVFJsYiAVlIxqx6pkTVVJeotLiKN91StINw5F151FqImT6EdaDNr0LuLZIB46p3D4-v3w8xdvyhF1a3alQy7-put-0l3tXtew3C3HDXkyUzSy050aBiSNmBcJHbV3YNwq8_joraFWAAhg_GSrOR5zf5m-ZkALKMgEAAA==) from code or binding the image element will also make it work, so it just breaks in the completely static case since nothing else generates the variable.
